=== [2] cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings ===
$ cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
Exit code: 1 — FAIL

Root causes (103 errors across integration test files only):
  - 84x non_snake_case: test function names like test_BC_HOOK_007_... use uppercase BC_HOOK
    (all in crates/monocle-test-harness/tests/ integration test files)
  - 2x unused-imports: NotificationPayload, PreToolUsePayload etc. imported but not directly used
    (integration_bc_hooks.rs:39, integration_payload.rs:26)
  - 12x expect_used / unwrap_err_used: .expect() and .unwrap_err() in test helper common/mod.rs
    and integration test bodies (clippy::expect_used deny in clippy.toml applies to test targets)

NOTE: Production source files (crates/monocle-test-harness/src/) pass clippy cleanly.
      All 103 errors are in integration test files. cargo test passes (155 tests, 0 failures).
      This is a test-naming convention issue (BC_HOOK uppercase in function names) + test helper
      utility code using .expect()/.unwrap_err() where clippy.toml bans them globally.

Adversary observation: clippy.toml applies -D expect_used to ALL targets including tests.
The test-writer should have added #[allow(clippy::expect_used)] to test helpers, or the
clippy.toml should use [profile.test] to relax expect_used for test targets only.

